Z||000000||Philphine||10-11-2000||12:53 PM||||<BR>i'm kinda sorta trying to look in the direction of a swap. at the moment i'm thinking a 4cam 3.4 with a 4:10 tranny. my first tranny feeler is for the tranny with the '84 cradle included. since '84 didn't have v6's should i bother with it or look for a later cradle to work with. this would go into a '87 4cyl. but i want to try to work with one cradle and swap out the whole thing. i probaly won't get anywhere with this but i want to get all the info i can scrape up. thanks for whatever you can tell me. ||||reg||1
Z||000001||StuGood||10-11-2000||10:50 PM||||I thought the 1984 through 1987 Fiero cradles were essentially the same.  <P>(Cue for <B>knowledgeable</B> Forum members to tell me I'm all wet...)   ||||reg||5
Z||000002||Xtreme Fiero's||10-11-2000||11:33 PM||||<BR> I was going to put a V6 in my first 84 about two years ago, from what I read ALL 84-87 Cradles are the same. ||||reg||1
Z||000003||Standard||10-12-2000||01:04 AM||||The 84's were a bit different in that they never had the v6 option.  I think they just don't have the bolt holes for the engine/tranny mounts drilled.  It would be a bit easier if you could get an 85 or later cradle.  Or just get an '88 cradle and transplant the '88 rear suspension along with it  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  a bit more work, tho.<P>------------------<BR>Mike -<BR>Black 86.5 GT 5 Spd, 151,000 miles and counting!         <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/BURNOUT.gif">      <BR>Red 84 Sport Coupe - winter donut maker   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/asthanos.gif"> ||||reg||1
